A.cards("c8s10",[{"id": "g8-10-standard", "h": "8.10 · Mechanisms and evidence", "c": ["c8-10-core"], "src": ["TB8:8.10"], "html": "<section class=\"e2-note-group\"><h4 class=\"e2-note-heading\">Rift a continent</h4><ul class=\"e2-note-points\"><li>Continental extension stretches and thins crust, commonly forming normal faults, tilted blocks, and grabens. Magma and warm fluids may accompany rifting. Extension and the pressure–temperature response vary from place to place during the evolution of a rift.</li></ul></section><section class=\"e2-note-group\"><h4 class=\"e2-note-heading\">Open an ocean basin</h4><ul class=\"e2-note-points\"><li>As continental rifting progresses to seafloor spreading, new oceanic crust forms at a ridge. Seawater can circulate through hot fractured rock and cause hydrothermal metamorphism. The hot-water pathway is especially important at mid-ocean ridges.</li></ul></section><section class=\"e2-note-group\"><h4 class=\"e2-note-heading\">Move horizontally on strike-slip faults</h4><ul class=\"e2-note-points\"><li>A strike-slip fault accommodates primarily horizontal relative motion. Looking across the fault, the opposite side moves right in a right-lateral fault and left in a left-lateral fault. Offset streams and roads preserve the displacement of originally continuous markers.</li></ul></section><section class=\"e2-note-group\"><h4 class=\"e2-note-heading\">Bends add local complexity</h4><ul class=\"e2-note-points\"><li>A bend or step in a strike-slip system can make adjacent rocks converge or pull apart. Local shortening can build folds and ridges, while local extension can produce a basin. The main lateral motion alone does not determine the sign of every bend.</li></ul></section><section class=\"e2-note-group\"><h4 class=\"e2-note-heading\">Key distinctions</h4><ul class=\"e2-note-points\"><li>Downdropped block during crustal extension → <mark class=\"e2-study-term\">Graben</mark>.</li><li>Circulation through hot oceanic rock → <mark class=\"e2-study-term\">Hydrothermal metamorphism</mark>.</li><li>Opposite side appears displaced right → <mark class=\"e2-study-term\">Right-lateral strike slip</mark>.</li><li>Opposite side appears displaced left → <mark class=\"e2-study-term\">Left-lateral strike slip</mark>.</li><li>Strike-slip step where blocks separate → <mark class=\"e2-study-term\">Releasing bend</mark>.</li></ul></section><details><summary>Original figures for this section</summary><figure><a href=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p2-Im1.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p2-Im1.png\" alt=\"Rift a continent · textbook section 8.10, PDF page 2\"></a><figcaption>Exploring Geology · 8.10 · PDF page 2 · original figure</figcaption></figure><figure><a href=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p3-Im1.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p3-Im1.png\" alt=\"Open an ocean basin · textbook section 8.10, PDF page 3\"></a><figcaption>Exploring Geology · 8.10 · PDF page 3 · original figure</figcaption></figure><figure><a href=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p4-Im3.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p4-Im3.png\" alt=\"Move horizontally on strike-slip faults · textbook section 8.10, PDF page 4\"></a><figcaption>Exploring Geology · 8.10 · PDF page 4 · original figure</figcaption></figure><figure><a href=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p5-Im3.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" src=\"assets/figures/chapter8-standard/8.10-p5-Im3.png\" alt=\"Bends add local complexity · textbook section 8.10, PDF page 5\"></a><figcaption>Exploring Geology · 8.10 · PDF page 5 · original figure</figcaption></figure></details>", "examId": "exam2", "traps": ["Use the observed geometry, rock properties and source-specific conditions before deciding on a process or history."], "media": []}]);
