A.teach("e2-c8-standard-10-write","c8-10-core","Explain rifting and ridge hydrothermal metamorphism, then describe one effect of a strike-slip bend.","Rifting stretches crust and can form normal faults and grabens. At a mid-ocean ridge, seawater circulates through hot fractured crust and alters it. A strike-slip bend can locally shorten rocks into ridges or extend them into a basin.",["Describes crustal extension and a structure.", "Locates hot-fluid alteration at a ridge.", "Explains circulation and heating.", "Describes a supported bend-related structure."],["TB8:8.10"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C8S10"], "focusedWriting": true});
