A.teach("e2-c8-standard-11-write","c8-11-core","Describe how thrusting can create folds, and explain how cleavage can help locate a fold hinge.","As layered rock moves over a bend in a thrust fault it can fold. Cleavage commonly parallels the axial surface and cuts bedding at changing angles across the fold; near the illustrated hinge it can be nearly perpendicular to bedding.",["Connects thrust movement to bending of layers.", "Identifies shortening or thrust-sheet stacking.", "Relates cleavage to the axial surface.", "Uses changing bedding–cleavage angles to identify fold geometry."],["TB8:8.11"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C8S11"], "focusedWriting": true});
