A.mc("e2-c8-standard-13-check","c8-13-core","An unfaulted lava flow covers a fault that offsets older sediment. What ordering is supported at this exposure?",["*The observed fault movement predates the lava flow|The unbroken flow seals the older fault movement.", "The lava flow predates the faulted sediment|The flow lies above and seals the older faulted strata.", "The flow must have been offset by the fault|The given flow is not offset.", "All events occurred at the same time|Cross-cutting and sealing establish a relative sequence."],"The unbroken flow seals the older fault movement.",["TB8:8.13"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C8S13"]});
A.teach("e2-c8-standard-13-write","c8-13-core","Explain how an offset bed and an unfaulted overlying flow constrain the age of fault motion.","The fault movement is younger than the bed it cuts. The unfaulted flow that seals the break is younger than the observed movement. Together they bracket the movement at that exposure without establishing an exact numerical date.",["States that the offset bed is older than movement.", "States that the sealing flow is younger than movement.", "Describes the age bracket.", "Keeps the conclusion limited to the observed movement."],["TB8:8.13"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C8S13"], "focusedWriting": true});
